From 64d672b2a93240f89121b0964635f319fa1309d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:20:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk/rm, wsi: scanout images come back when the host releases
 them

KMD 22.22.315 on a host with NVGPU_F_SCANOUT_RELEASE (feature bit 15)
tracks when the host is done with a flipped image
(guest/windows/docs/foreign-scanout.md, "Buffer release"):
SCANOUT_STATUS (op 12) answers the released floor of a DRM handle (every
flip with seq <= it is done; skipped and dropped fenced presents count as
done), and the SCANOUT_RELEASED event (kind 3, handle 0) rings whenever it
may have moved.  QueryCaps.supported_ops bit 35 says so.

Until now the Win32 scanout swapchain handed an image back a fixed two
presents after it was shown, a guess that can tear.  With the capability:

- nvk/rm: every flip through the KMD's source records its out_seq on the
  memory (plain and fenced SCANOUT_PRESENT; the flip thread's flips record
  it when sent, and a memory with flips still queued there has no seq yet,
  so a wait on it first waits for the thread).
  nvkmd_rm_mem_scanout_wait_released() waits until the floor reaches the
  memory's latest seq: librmclient's crm_win_scanout_wait_released (reset
  the event, ask, then wait: no lost wake), at most the caller's timeout,
  and at most 1 s; past the host's own 500 ms forced release the image is
  written anyway and counted.  A transport that went away counts as done.
- wsi/win32: wsi_device::win32.scanout_wait_released (optional; called
  with VK_NULL_HANDLE at swapchain creation to ask whether it works).  A
  scanout swapchain with it hands an image back as soon as a later one is
  shown, marked release-pending; acquire picks the idle image shown
  longest ago and waits for its release outside the lock (VK_TIMEOUT /
  VK_NOT_READY within the app's timeout, the image then stays idle).
  Without it: the old two-presents rule, unchanged.
- librmclient: crm_win_scanout_status, crm_win_scanout_wait_released
  (loaded as optional symbols).

NVK_SCANOUT_RELEASE=0 keeps the old rule.

win11, KMD 22.22.312 (no capability): "not tracked", vk_scanout_present
1920x1080 with two and three images as before (6400 / 6160 fps, 0
failed, 0 release waits).  The tracked path needs KMD 22.22.315 and a
backend with feature bit 15.

Order: after 0030 (presents on RM fences), before patches-windows-dxvk/.
